pend new configuration and activate it as latest.','Replace commitment voting set; start/stop replication for all members; rollback latest when truncating its suffix.'],\n implementation_guards=['Leader accepts changes only with latest=committed and current-term entry committed; optional prevIndex must match current latest index.'],important_branches=['AddVoter directly creates Voter in current code; no staging catch-up phase in this path.','Nonvoters are replicated to but excluded from commitment, election request set and lease tally.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Changes which match indexes qualify for advancement.','A2':'Changes campaign and vote eligibility; committing local removal ends authority.'},unknowns=['Live role/address change effects on already pending verification futures remain a separate question.'])\nbeh('B-startup','A6','BootstrapCluster and NewRaft before workers start','Stored current term, snapshot metadata and suffix logs','Fresh bootstrap or process startup',['S-bootstrap','S-startup','S-config-replay','S-store','S-stable'],\n durable_effects=['Bootstrap requires clean state, persists term 1 and configuration entry 1.'],writes=['Initialize follower; load current term and last log; restore latest usable snapshot, then scan suffix for configurations.'],important_branches=['Snapshot failure falls back to older snapshots; failure of every available snapshot rejects startup.','NoSnapshotRestoreOnStart skips FSM restore while restoring metadata.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Persisted log/snapshot prefix remains available for later replication and commitment reconstruction.','A2':'Persisted term and vote keys constrain subsequent elections; startup does not claim leadership.'},unknowns=['Concrete storage backend crash guarantees and external FSM startup restoration are not validated.'])\nbeh('B-snapshot','A3','Leader replication worker, receiver main loop, receiver FSM worker','Snapshot index/term/configuration and leader term','Missing log triggers snapshot transfer; InstallSnapshot processing',['S-snapshot-send','S-install','S-fsm'],\n produces_fact_ids=['F-stored-support','F-peer-positive'],\n implementation_guards=['Reject old request term or invalid snapshot version; require complete byte count, successful sink close and FSM restoration.','Sender rejects higher response term before updating match; requires Success.'],writes=['Receiver records restored lastApplied/snapshot/configurations and compacts or removes old logs; sender advances nextIndex and reports snapshot index match.'],external_effects=['Successful sender processing notifies pending verification futures true.'],important_branches=['Transfer/storage/restore errors prevent successful acknowledgement; compaction errors are logged after successful restore.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Snapshot success contributes the snapshot index to voter-filtered commitment.','A2':'Restored configuration and snapshot log term affect subsequent eligibility and election freshness.'},unknowns=['Delayed snapshot installation relative to newer committed state needs its own legal-history investigation.'])\nbeh('B-snapshot-save','A6','Snapshot worker with FSM and main-loop requests','FSM snapshot index/term and committed configuration index','Periodic or user snapshot request',['S-snapshot','S-fsm'],\n durable_effects=['Persist and close snapshot before recording snapshot metadata and compacting logs.'],implementation_guards=['Reject when FSM snapshot index precedes committed configuration index.'],cross_activity_effects={'A3':'Provides snapshot producer for resynchronization and startup.','A1':'Preserves application prefix plus committed membership metadata after log compaction.'})\nbeh('B-transfer','A2','Leader main loop, transfer goroutine, target TimeoutNow handler','Selected peer replication progress and transfer lifetime','LeadershipTransfer request',['S-leader-loop','S-transfer','S-transfer-trigger','S-candidate'],\n consumes_fact_ids=['F-authority'],writes=['Block new apply/config/restore while transfer is in progress; await replication nextIndex beyond lastIndex then send TimeoutNow.','Target becomes candidate with transfer flag, bypasses prevote; flag cleared at candidate-loop exit.'],important_branches=['Automatic target selection filters voters; explicit target requires replication state.','Transfer timeout or leader-loop exit controls future completion; a sent TimeoutNow alone is not evidence of election success.'],existing_protections=['Actual election still tallies voters and validates log freshness.'])\nbeh('B-user-restore','A3','Leader loop and FSM worker; offline RecoverCluster caller','Explicit disaster-recovery operation, not normal commit history','Restore or offline RecoverCluster',['S-user-restore','S-api-restore','S-recovery'],\n writes=['Online restore aborts inflight logs, creates snapshot at larger index in current term/current configuration, restores FSM, then public API submits a no-op and waits.','Offline RecoverCluster replays stored command suffix, snapshots supplied configuration, deletes old log range.'],important_branches=['Online restore rejects outstanding configuration change; public API warns this is for disaster recovery into a fresh cluster.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Exceptional restore can replace state outside ordinary command commitment; must be explicitly excluded or modeled in an ordinary safety check.','A7':'Inflight commands return ErrAbortedByRestore.'})\nbeh('B-heartbeat','A2','Independent heartbeat goroutine per replication worker','Worker-captured term and peer; map of pending verification futures','Periodic or forced heartbeat response',['S-heartbeat','S-repl'],\n consumes_fact_ids=['F-append-success'],produces_fact_ids=['F-peer-positive'],\n writes=['On error-free transport return update lastContact and call notifyAll(resp.Success).'],important_branches=['Transport errors back off; stop channel ends worker.','Unlike ordinary replication this branch does not compare resp.Term to req.Term.','Heartbeat contains no log prefix or leader commit index.'],existing_protections=['Receiver rejects stale-term heartbeat; false success flag becomes negative verification notification.'],unknowns=['A positive reply may have been produced before future registration; no operation ID appears in the RPC.'])\nbeh('B-verify-register','A2','Leader main loop','One verifyFuture, quorum from latest voter count','VerifyLeader future received with quorumSize=0',['S-api-verify','S-verify-register','S-leader','S-lease'],\n consumes_fact_ids=['F-authority'],writes=['Initialize votes=1 and voter-derived quorum; register future in every replication worker notify map; force heartbeats.'],important_branches=['Single-voter quorum completes immediately.','Registration loop has no suffrage filter; replState includes nonvoters.'],unknowns=['Whether nonvoter support can suffice for externally successful verification during loss of voter contact is the selected discriminator.'])\nbeh('B-verify-notify','A2','Replication, snapshot or heartbeat goroutine; verifyFuture vote lock','Pending future pointer in one peer notify map','notifyAll(true/false) after response handling',['S-repl','S-repl-update','S-heartbeat','S-snapshot-send','S-verify-vote'],\n consumes_fact_ids=['F-peer-positive'],produces_fact_ids=['F-verify-threshold'],writes=['Swap out the peer notify map under lock; for each registered future call vote(bool).','Positive increments votes; threshold enqueues future to main loop and clears notifyCh; negative also enqueues and clears.'],important_branches=['Vote receives only bool, no peer ID, suffrage, response term or originating RPC identity.','Once notifyCh is nil subsequent vote calls do not change the tally.'],existing_protections=['Per-peer map clearing and future vote lock prevent repeated votes through the same drained registration.'],unknowns=['Interaction with concurrent registrations/removal deserves a separate scope from fixed membership.'])\nbeh('B-verify-finish','A2','Leader main loop','Same verifyFuture pointer and retained threshold','Returned future arrives on verifyCh',['S-leader-loop','S-leader','S-follower','S-candidate'],\n consumes_fact_ids=['F-verify-threshold'],external_effects=['At threshold respond nil; below threshold step down and return ErrNotLeader; remove future from leader and peer maps.'],important_branches=['Leader exit fails pending futures with ErrLeadershipLost; follower/candidate returns ErrNotLeader.'],cross_activity_effects={'A7':'Public completion is used by callers to decide whether local reads may be stale, per API documentation.'})\nF=[]\ndef fact(id,meaning,identity,ctx,rep,ss,dur='Volatile observation; no separate durability claim.',rec='Re-established by executing the producing path in a new context.',**kw):\n d=dict(id=id,meaning=meaning,identity=identity,validity_context=ctx,representation=rep,durability=dur,recovery=rec,source_ids=ss);d.update(kw);F.append(d)\nfact('F-stored-support','The leader recorded this server as matching through index i after local storage success, successful nonempty append response, or successful snapshot response.',{'server':'ServerID','history':'captured leader commitment object','index':'matched log or snapshot index'},'Eligible to advance only if ID is in commitment.matchIndexes; support tied to a leadership object, not globally reusable.',['commitment.matchIndexes'],['S-commit','S-dispatch','S-repl-update','S-snapshot-send'],dur='Recorded matches are volatile; backing log/snapshot persistence relies on supplied stores.',invalidators=['B-authority-life'],reinterpreters=['B-membership'],unknowns=['Storage backend crash behavior remains outside this map.'])\nfact('F-append-success','The receiver completed the checks and writes applicable to this AppendEntries request and set Success=true; an empty heartbeat establishes no replicated log prefix.',{'rpc':'request/response pair supplied by Transport','term':'request term','peer':'receiver'},'Meaning depends on presence of PrevLogEntry and Entries; response delivery and consumption occur later.',['AppendEntriesResponse.Success'],['S-append','S-transport'],unknowns=['No transport-level message identity or Byzantine authenticity guarantee inferred.'])\nfact('F-leader-commit','For this leadership commitment object the voter majority match position advanced to i at or beyond startIndex, and main loop consumes that bound for prefix processing.',{'leader':'local server and leadership period','index':'commit bound'},'Current configured voter map; previously committed prefix is carried by logs/snapshot, not old worker counters.',['commitment.commitIndex','Raft commitIndex'],['S-commit','S-leader-loop'],dur='Commit counter is volatile; replicated log and snapshot are the durable backing.',rec='New leader reconfirms through a current-term entry; followers consume leader commit bound.',unknowns=['Follower receipt of a bound is not an independent reconstruction of its quorum proof.'])\nfact('F-application','The FSM callback for a committed command has returned and the matching ApplyFuture response has been populated before success notification.',{'operation':'logFuture pointer','log':'term/index assigned to command'},'Normal Apply path; excludes disaster recovery replacement.',['logFuture.response','future error channel'],['S-fsm','S-process','S-future'],dur='FSM durability depends on caller implementation; future completion itself is volatile.')\nfact('F-vote','A voter grant for requested term and candidate has been returned after persisted vote checks/writes, or the candidate has persisted its self-vote.',{'term':'requested election term','candidate':'encoded candidate address','voter':'contacted ServerID'},'Real election, separate from pre-vote; candidate IDs additionally checked on modern requests.',['RequestVoteResponse.Granted','stable last-vote keys'],['S-vote','S-election-send'],dur='Term and candidate are separate stable-store writes; atomicity across them is not asserted.',rec='RequestVote consults persisted keys on later requests.',unknowns=['Partial stable-store failure/crash between writes is not modeled.'])\nfact('F-authority','The local candidate received enough granted real-election results on its attempt channel to enter Leader state.',{'server':'local ServerID','term':'currentTerm','attempt':'voteCh instance'},'Local role acquisition; does not itself assert continuing external authority after a partition.',['Raft state Leader','leader ID/address'],['S-candidate','S-election-send'],invalidators=['B-authority-life','B-transfer'])\nfact('F-peer-positive','A replication worker dispatched a positive verification notification because an error-free heartbeat response had Success=true, or a successful append/snapshot path called notifyAll(true). This is not itself a voter-qualified or operation-fresh quorum assertion.',{'worker':'followerReplication pointer for remote member','context':'captured leadership term and pending notify-map contents'},'Notification targets futures present when notifyAll drains its map; positive carries no responder suffrage, RPC identity or production time to vote().',['notifyAll(true)','verifyFuture.vote(true)'],['S-repl-update','S-snapshot-send','S-heartbeat','S-repl'],unknowns=['Same-history correlation of request production, reply delivery and future registration has not been executed.'])\nfact('F-verify-threshold','The future has accumulated its numeric quorum threshold of positive votes (including initialized self vote) and was enqueued for completion.',{'operation':'verifyFuture pointer'},'A threshold result is distinct from a negative wake-up on the same channel; both are checked by leaderLoop.',['verifyFuture.votes >= verifyFuture.quorumSize'],['S-verify-register','S-verify-vote','S-leader-loop'],unknowns=['Threshold does not encode the identities or suffrage of contributing peers.'])\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nactivity_summaries={\n'A1':('Replicate and commit ordered commands','Apply, appendEntries, replicateTo, commitment.match/recalculate; voter match aggregation and startIndex condition.'),\n'A2':('Acquire and maintain valid authority','Follower timeout, optional prevote, durable election, role lifecycle, VerifyLeader and transfer.'),\n'A3':('Restore eligible state','InstallSnapshot and snapshot transfer repair missing history; explicit disaster recovery replaces state under a distinct contract.'),\n'A4':('Determine eligible participants','Latest/committed configurations, voter suffrage, serialized changes and rollback on log truncation.'),\n'A5':('Apply decisions','processLogs and runFSM separate commit/enqueue from callback and future completion.'),\n'A6':('Persist and reconstruct supporting history','LogStore/StableStore, startup replay and snapshots; concrete backend durability remains open.'),\n'A7':('Admit and complete client operations','Apply/Future, VerifyLeader, Barrier and recovery APIs expose distinct completion meanings.')}\nactivities=[]\nfor a,(purpose,summary) in activity_summaries.items():\n ss=sorted({s for b in B if b['primary_activity']==a for s in b['source_ids']})\n activities.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=purpose,realization_summary=summary,source_ids=ss))\ndef path(expl,bs,fs):\n return dict(explanation=expl,behavior_ids=bs,fact_ids=fs,source_ids=sorted({s for b in B if b['id'] in bs for s in b['source_ids']}))\nformation=path('Apply creates a future and queues a command. Only the leader dispatches it, assigns term/index, calls StoreLogs and reports its own match. Per-peer workers send predecessor-qualified appends; followers reject stale terms or mismatching prefixes, truncate conflicting suffixes and store new entries before success. Ordinary and pipeline consumers use the corresponding request to report the last appended index; snapshot completion is an alternate support producer. commitment filters ServerIDs to latest voters, takes the majority match position and requires reaching the first index of this term. The main loop records commitment, processes the prefix and sends commit tuples to the FSM worker. runFSM completes command futures after callbacks. Later appends carry the commit bound to followers. Empty heartbeat success establishes contact without a replicated prefix. Store errors, retry/backoff, higher terms and shutdown take distinct paths.', ['B-api','B-dispatch','B-append','B-repl','B-commit','B-apply','B-snapshot'],['F-stored-support','F-append-success','F-leader-commit','F-application'])\ncontext=path('Bootstrap persists initial term/configuration; NewRaft restores term, snapshot and configuration suffix before starting follower/FSM/snapshot workers. A voting follower with expired contact becomes candidate, optionally prevotes, then electSelf persists the new term and own vote and contacts latest voters. Vote handlers check leader, membership, term, prior vote and log freshness; majority grants on an attempt-local channel establish the local Leader role. Entry allocates new commitment/replication state and appends a no-op. Higher-term RPCs, higher-term data replies, loss of voter contact and committed removal can end leadership; cleanup stops replication and fails remaining inflight/verify futures. Transfer pauses writes, catches up a selected peer, sends TimeoutNow and still requires a real election. Verification is an additional public authority check based on asynchronous peer notifications, not the commit counter.', ['B-startup','B-elect','B-vote','B-authority-life','B-transfer','B-verify-register','B-heartbeat','B-verify-notify','B-verify-finish'],['F-vote','F-authority','F-peer-positive','F-verify-threshold'])\nconnection=path('Stored log/snapshot history survives leadership loss, but match tallies and response channels do not transfer into the next leader object. New authority uses log freshness in elections and a current-term startIndex/no-op to reconfirm advancement over old entries. Old replication workers retain old commitment/stepDown pointers; old election replies remain on old attempt channels. Remaining inflight calls fail on exit, whereas already queued committed FSM work may finish. Membership affects elections, commitment and leases via latest voter eligibility; configuration changes require stable prior membership and a current-term commit, and truncation can roll latest back. Snapshots bind an applied prefix to committed membership and reconstruct it at startup or resynchronization. Disaster recovery is explicitly exceptional and not interchangeable with normal Apply. VerifyLeader consumes response notifications through a separate boolean tally; its voter-eligibility and freshness meaning must be investigated rather than borrowed from commitment.', ['B-authority-life','B-membership','B-startup','B-snapshot','B-snapshot-save','B-user-restore','B-verify-register','B-verify-notify','B-verify-finish','B-apply'],['F-stored-support','F-leader-commit','F-authority','F-peer-positive','F-application'])\nmapdata=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured HashiCorp Raft library: main role loop, per-peer replication/heartbeat workers, FSM worker, snapshot worker and caller-supplied stores/transport/FSM. No deployment-specific application or crash-durable backend has been executed.',protocol_contexts=['ServerID and address','currentTerm and election attempt','latest versus committed configuration indexes','term/index log identity','per-leadership commitment object','public future identity'],external_interfaces=['Apply/Barrier/VerifyLeader','configuration changes','BootstrapCluster/NewRaft','Restore/RecoverCluster','Transport','LogStore/StableStore/SnapshotStore','FSM/BatchingFSM/ConfigurationStore'],ownership=['Main loop owns role/configuration/inflight state','Replication workers own peer progress with shared locked commitment','FSM worker serializes application and restore'],selection_injection=['Caller supplies transport, stores, FSM and validated configuration; in-repository transport/storage implementations are not presumed externalized.'],variants=['Pre-vote optional by config/transport','Protocol compatibility branches','Pipelined versus ordinary replication','Single versus batching FSM','Optional monotonic log store','Optional fast heartbeat transport callback'],source_ids=['S-startup','S-transport','S-store','S-stable','S-fsm-contract'],unknowns=['No deployment authentication or fault model has been established.','No separately accessible guide.md was found in the authorized source/support trees; the supplied method and JSON schemas define this submission.']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,\n core_overview=dict(formation=formation,context=context,connection=connection,status='usable',rationale='Both core paths and the connecting ownership, eligibility, persistence, old-work and completion mechanisms have been traced through actual callers and consumers. Usable means sufficient source backbone to select a local discriminator; no execution, broad safety conclusion or complete coverage is asserted.',core_gaps=[],open_details=['Concrete transport pipeline error propagation and optional concurrent fast-heartbeat path.','Crash atomicity/durability and storage failure recovery variants.','Live membership mutation during pending verification.','Delayed snapshot ordering against newer committed state.','Historical membership.md is a proposal: its staging AddVoter and committed GetConfiguration descriptions differ from current code; use current interface/code for applicability.']),\n surfaces=[dict(entry_point='VerifyLeader -> verifyLeader -> notifyAll -> vote -> leaderLoop',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-verify-register','B-heartbeat','B-verify-notify','B-verify-finish'],reason='Selected next discriminator: voter-count threshold is fed by registrations on all replication peers. Need applicable contract and actual same-history completion before asserting a defect.',source_ids=['S-api-verify','S-verify-register','S-verify-vote','S-leader','S-heartbeat'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='heartbeat versus replicateTo higher-term handling',disposition='deferred',behavior_ids=['B-heartbeat','B-repl','B-authority-life'],reason='Heartbeat updates contact and forwards Success without the higher-term guard used by data replication. Lease checks and negative verify notifications are contrary protections; consequences require a controlled actual history.',source_ids=['S-heartbeat','S-repl','S-lease'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='installSnapshot delayed request',disposition='deferred',behavior_ids=['B-snapshot'],reason='Snapshot restore changes application progress and membership; ordering relative to a newer committed prefix has not been checked. Requires a legal producer history and snapshot endpoint.',source_ids=['S-install','S-snapshot-send'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='NetworkTransport fast heartbeat and pipeline implementations',disposition='UNCLASSIFIED_PROTOCOL_RESPONSIBILITY',reason='Transport interface admits a callback concurrent with blocking work; concrete implementation must be read before attributing synchronization guarantees.',source_ids=['S-transport','S-startup'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='StableStore partial write failure',disposition='deferred',behavior_ids=['B-vote','B-startup'],reason='Vote persistence uses two writes; interface does not state cross-key transactionality. A specific backend and permitted crash/error model are needed.',source_ids=['S-election-send','S-stable'],high_consequence=True)])\nPath('audit-map.json').write_text(json.dumps(mapdata,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nquestion=dict(question='Can positive notifications from nonvoting replication peers satisfy a VerifyLeader future under fixed mixed membership without the voter support required for that public authority check?',importance='VerifyLeader is documented as preventing stale local FSM reads after leadership loss. If nonvoter support can substitute for an authority-confirming voter quorum, public success may mislead a read caller. This question does not yet establish a stale application read or an incorrect log decision.',source_ids=['S-api-verify','S-config-contract','S-verify-register','S-verify-vote','S-leader-loop','S-leader','S-repl','S-heartbeat','S-repl-update','S-snapshot-send','S-lease'],participants=['leader','voting followers','nonvoting followers','VerifyLeader caller'],objects=['verifyFuture','per-peer notify map','latest Configuration'],contexts=['fixed mixed voter/nonvoter membership','one actual leadership period','one VerifyLeader invocation through public completion'],event_paths=['bootstrap and actual election -> stable configuration -> VerifyLeader registration -> actual peer response production/delivery -> notifyAll -> vote -> leaderLoop future completion'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B-repl','B-snapshot','B-heartbeat','B-verify-register','B-verify-notify','B-verify-finish'],fact_ids=['F-peer-positive'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-membership':'Defines actual voter/nonvoter roles and replication eligibility.','B-elect':'Establishes a real leader before the check.','B-authority-life':'Lease expiry, higher-term stepdown and cleanup are protective competing events.','B-commit':'Shows separately voter-filtered log commitment; its guarantees cannot be assumed for VerifyLeader.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['VerifyLeader returns errors on follower/candidate and on negative notification; leader exit fails pending verification.','Voter-only lease checks can end authority even if nonvoters respond.','Normal commitment explicitly excludes nonvoter matches; no incorrect log commitment follows from this registration asymmetry alone.','The API does not literally state a voter-quorum formula; its authority/read purpose needs a justified requirement derivation.'],unknowns=['Applicable requirement: derive the necessary support condition for this authority API without turning implementation asymmetry into its own oracle.','Actual producer: execute actual nonvoter reply production and its consumption, not a synthetic vote(bool).','Initial prefix: observe real election and settled mixed membership with public configuration and committed operation.','Same execution: exclude old voter replies as contributors, retain negative replies/lease/stepdown workers, and correlate the checked future interval.','Observed endpoint: measure the same public future result; stale FSM read and newer-leader application are separate unobserved consequences.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Source trace found verifyLeader registers every replState entry, while quorumSize counts voters; vote receives no peer identity/suffrage. This concrete producer-consumer relation makes eligibility the best next discriminator. A fixed configuration bounds configuration-transition ambiguity.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nsubmission=dict(action='continue',rationale='Register the initial two-core-path map and continue with the eligibility meaning of positive verification support. Among the sourced frontier options, fixed-membership VerifyLeader eligibility has a concrete public endpoint and controllable real reply producers; heartbeat higher-term/contact semantics additionally requires timing and term-transition analysis; snapshot ordering requires a longer generated prefix. First resolve the authority-check requirement and isolate actual nonvoter contributions while retaining lease and negative-response protections. No obligation or evidence is claimed by this source-only product.',sources=sources,map_path='audit-map.json',question=question)\nPath('submission.json').write_text(json.dumps(submission,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 build_submission.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\ns=json.load(open('submission.json'));m=json.load(open('audit-map.json'))\njsonsch